%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against services/brief/builder.py + D74 (which REVERSED D20's
%% display gating) + D16 + D53 + B5
flowchart TB
    SNAP[("frozen ContextSnapshot<br/><b>holds EVERYTHING</b> - policy numbers,<br/>every Coverage figure")]:::snap
    ID["IdentityResolution<br/>assurance level"]:::id

    SNAP --> G1
    ID --> G1

    G1{"<b>may_see_record</b><br/>is there anybody to show?<br/>= assurance is L1 or better"}:::gate
    G1 -- "NO — L0 only" --> L0["<b>NOTHING RENDERS</b><br/>no name, no policy, no history.<br/>Not a restriction: at L0 there is<br/>simply nobody to render."]:::low
    G1 -- "YES — L1, L2, L3" --> G2

    G2{"<b>may_act_on_policy</b><br/>may they SAY it and DO it?<br/>= assurance is L2 or better"}:::gate

    G2 -- "NO — L1" --> L1["<b>SHOWN, BUT NOT YET USABLE</b><br/>- policy number IS on screen<br/>- coverage figures ARE on screen<br/>- number carries a standing note:<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;'(ยังไม่ยืนยันตัวตน — ยังใช้/อ้างอิงกับผู้ติดต่อไม่ได้)'<br/>- verify-identity PREPENDED as action 0<br/>- every playbook step above L1 DROPPED<br/>- opening line asks an OPEN question, no name (D55)<br/>- degraded = LOW_ASSURANCE"]:::mid
    G2 -- "YES — L2 / L3" --> L2["<b>FULL USE</b><br/>- read the number aloud<br/>- confirm a figure<br/>- change a detail, process a claim<br/>- full playbook"]:::high

    L1 --> PROMO["agent attests on the call (D42):<br/>Confirmed, or a verified third party (D65)"]:::promo
    PROMO --> L2
    PROMO -.-> NOTE["<b>this is a RE-RENDER, not a re-fetch.</b><br/>The data was already in memory.<br/>No round trip to the bank core.<br/>Assurance moves DOWN this way too."]:::note

    D74["<b>D74 reversed D20 here, and it matters.</b> The old rule hid<br/>the record below L2. But the agent needs the record precisely<br/>SO THAT they can verify the caller — hiding it makes<br/>verification impossible, and showing a bank employee the<br/>record they were routed is internal processing, not<br/>disclosure. So assurance gates what the agent may SAY and DO,<br/>never what they may SEE."]:::big

    L1 --> WIRE
    L2 --> WIRE
    L0 --> WIRE
    WIRE["<b>GATE AT THE WIRE, SERVER-SIDE</b><br/>BriefOut is a wire DTO, never CaseBrief.model_dump().<br/>Shipping the domain model and hiding fields in React<br/>is defeated by devtools — and it shipped a real leak (B5, D53)."]:::wire
    WIRE --> V2["CaseBrief v2 (versioned, never mutated - D7)"]:::v2

    B5["<b>gate the SENTENCE on the identity, not the payload.</b><br/>After a rejection the frozen snapshot still holds the old<br/>policy, so a summary built from the payload will happily print<br/>a number the structured fields correctly withheld. Both<br/>`may_see` and `may_act_on_policy` come from the IdentityResolution."]:::note

    NO_AI["<b>the LLM is not even imported here (D16)</b><br/>every figure is read from a typed Coverage field,<br/>so there is no code path that could put an<br/>invented number on an insurance screen"]:::note

